CloudBurrow patch 26 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1235). Applies after patch 0025.

The bug: IntValue's EQ, GT, GTE, LT and LTE compared an INT64 with a FLOAT64
by converting the float with ToInt64, which truncates: 2 = 2.5 was true, and
the conversion of an infinity is implementation-specific in Go (MinInt64 on
amd64, MaxInt64 on arm64). UNNEST reads an array through JSON (patch 0025),
which writes FLOAT64 2.0 as 2, so its elements come back as INT64 and MAX
compares IntValue(2) with +Inf: on amd64 SELECT MAX(x) FROM
UNNEST([CAST('inf' AS FLOAT64), 2.0]) AS x answered 2, not +Inf. The patch
compares an IntValue with a FloatValue as float64, as BigQuery compares
INT64 with FLOAT64. value_int_float_compare_test.go fails without the patch
and passes with it; inf_unnest_test.go's MAX case now passes on amd64.

